WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:08.017
In this video, we'll steer the
four sessions while they build,

2
00:00:08.017 --> 00:00:12.334
tour the Sessions list, and switch
between the four toolbars in one lab.

3
00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:14.912
This is a real run, with the waits sped up.

4
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.892
Open one of the running sessions.

5
00:00:17.892 --> 00:00:21.426
To change its course mid-run, type a message,

6
00:00:21.426 --> 00:00:25.195
and in the Send menu,
choose Steer with Message.

7
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:34.875
This one asks for a tooltip on every button,
with its name and keyboard shortcut.

8
00:00:34.875 --> 00:00:37.569
It reaches the session after its next step.

9
00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:43.908
In another session, Add to Queue
waits until the session is done.

10
00:00:43.908 --> 00:00:47.822
This one asks for three bullets on
what makes the toolbar different.

11
00:00:51.692 --> 00:00:54.663
You can also steer with a
design note of your own.

12
00:00:54.663 --> 00:00:57.278
Here, make the selected tool easier to spot.

13
00:01:01.872 --> 00:01:03.884
The Sessions list keeps it tidy.

14
00:01:03.884 --> 00:01:08.223
Collapse the main session to tuck
the four away, and expand it again.

15
00:01:12.297 --> 00:01:16.186
Each one shows its status as it works.
Pin the ones you care about.

16
00:01:21.407 --> 00:01:24.716
As each one finishes,
it reports back to the main session.

17
00:01:28.569 --> 00:01:32.200
From a session's menu,
Mark as Done sets it aside.

18
00:01:36.819 --> 00:01:40.719
Here are the three bullets the
queued message asked for: every tool

19
00:01:40.719 --> 00:01:44.561
visible, shortcuts in plain sight,
and fewer clicks to draw again.

20
00:01:50.141 --> 00:01:53.968
While the main session builds the lab,
it checks every toolbar in the browser.

21
00:01:57.144 --> 00:01:59.908
When all four are done,
the main session builds the lab,

22
00:01:59.908 --> 00:02:02.623
and gives you the link and
a summary of each direction.

23
00:02:03.344 --> 00:02:06.276
It even suggests a pick,
but the call is yours.

24
00:02:10.878 --> 00:02:13.476
The lab opens on Playful and expressive,

25
00:02:13.476 --> 00:02:16.788
a hand-drawn palette that
says what each tool does.

26
00:02:20.808 --> 00:02:24.868
Every toolbar still draws.
Try one, to feel how it works.

27
00:02:31.183 --> 00:02:36.195
Switch with the pill or the
bracket keys: Big and touch

28
00:02:36.195 --> 00:02:40.933
friendly, the original,
Dense, Minimal, and Playful.

29
00:02:47.374 --> 00:02:50.551
Back to Big and touch friendly, my pick.

30
00:02:50.551 --> 00:02:55.555
Large, labeled buttons in a dock,
where a thumb can reach them.
